  "slug": "classification-single-gene-set-2d4b",
  "summary": "Five preprints use structured latent and mixture models to separate heritable, environmental, and donor effects in single-cell and lineage-resolved data.",
  "synthesis": "The items share a focus on structured models that partition variation in single-cell data into interpretable sources. scPACE uses a hierarchical personalized variational autoencoder to represent cell and donor states in cohort transcriptomics and to impute missing cell types. SOUR separates heritable lineage effects from spatial microenvironment effects on tumor cell expression. ChronoClone groups clones into metaclones by time-resolved cell-state composition, revealing differences in clonal speed. ELLA-mix applies a count-conditioned finite mixture to identify cell subpopulations with distinct radial RNA localization in imaging-based spatial data. PRNODE jointly estimates mother and daughter yeast protein networks with a shared scaffold to quantify inheritance. The common emphasis is explicit modeling of inheritance, environment, and subcellular or temporal structure, rather than large pretrained embeddings alone.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-26"
}
